 "notes": [
  "Byte provenance: pins.oracle.path ('Binaries/NxPhysics.dll') is ABSENT from this checkout and no workspace file carries the pinned identity (size 1253376, sha256 4b7db3e126735c57...). The only NxPhysics.dll present (build/Release/NxPhysics.dll, 37,376 bytes, different digest) was NOT used. Full slot lists were rebuilt from docs/reconstruction/novodex-physics/oracle/pe.json 'pointers' (21844 decoded pointer records mapping slot RVA -> target RVA), which the Phase 1 oracle census extracted from the pinned image itself.",
  "Inclusion rule: every data_objects row of type 'dispatch_table' whose REBUILT full target list contains at least one RVA exactly matching a functions row with phase==5. 5 of 131 dispatch_table rows qualify (phys_data_000678, _000679, _000842, _000976, _000979). Restricting the rule to the recorded notes-blob previews would admit only 4: 74 of the 131 rows record just their first 8 targets, which hides phys_data_000842 (its first 8 slots are pure-call filler; its phase-5 hits begin at slot 12).",
  "Validation: every row's first min(recorded, slots) rebuilt targets equal the recorded preview (0 mismatches; re-checked from the saved output: 0 bad). Total declared slots across all 131 rows = 2437, matching oracle/data-coverage.json's 'pointer_table_slots': 2437 exactly.",
  "Slot resolution is exact RVA match against inventory functions; fn_id=null marks an RVA with no function row, target=null marks a slot with no recovered pointer record. Every slot of every qualifying table resolved (no unrecovered slots).",
  "Family grouping (|A n B| / min(|A|,|B|) of distinct targets > 0.60): NO family components emerged. Closest pair is phys_data_000678/phys_data_000679 sharing only 2 distinct targets (ratio 0.500 against the smaller set); the five qualifying tables are structurally independent vtables, not base/derived replicas.",
  "Largest pair read. 0x001043d0 (phys_data_000678, 87 slots) is interface-SHAPED: slot 0 -> phys_fn_000042 (0x00002460, phase 5), slots 63/64 -> phys_fn_000038/_000040 (0x00002400/0x00002430, phase 5), and the other 84 slots all point at phys_fn_005667 (0x000f41dc, a 20-byte phase-8 runtime-tail compiler artifact acting as the pure-call filler). 0x00104530 (phys_data_000679, 88 slots) is fully implemented: 88 distinct targets, ALL 88 resolving to phase-5 function rows. Only slots 63/64 are identical between them. oracle/ghidra/manifest.json corroborates the pairing: ctor FUN_10002480 stores PTR_LAB_101043d0 while ctor FUN_10003650 stores PTR_FUN_10104530. Reading: 0x1043d0 is the abstract actor-interface vtable and 0x104530 the concrete dynamic-actor implementation; the body layer contributes the single extra tail slot rather than a third table.",
  "non_phase5_target_histogram counts slot OCCURRENCES (not distinct targets) over all included tables. 100 of the 111 non-phase-5 occurrences are the single pure-call filler phys_fn_005667 (phase 8): 84 in phys_data_000678, 12 in phys_data_000842, 4 in phys_data_000976. Genuine cross-phase borrowings are thin: phase 3 x6, phase 7 x3, phase 2 x1, phase 6 x1. Both large tables are therefore essentially phase-5-owned once filler is discounted.",
  "Shape-run observation. The five per-type shape vtables from evidence/phase3-narrow-phase.md L552-L560 sit inside one contiguous .rdata run together with phys_data_000842 @ 0x00106a58 (declared 41 slots, size 164): BOX @ 0x106ab8 is exactly 24 slots into that run, and BOX's slot 5 (0x00020880 / phys_fn_000949, the sole phase-5 raycast partner Phase 3 identified) appears at index 5+24=29 of phys_data_000842, with BOX slot 7 (0x00020b20 / phys_fn_000951) likewise at index 31. Caveat flagged for Phase 5 owners: a 41-slot table at 0x106a58 would overrun BOX @ +24 slots, so either the declared 41 covers a merged multi-class pointer run (constructors storing interior offsets) or the BOX extent (17 slots here, derived heuristically from consecutive pe.json pointer records because BOX has NO inventory dispatch_table row) is short. Resolve from the five shape ctors' vtable stores before relying on extents.",
  "vtable slot 7 (the continuous-collision sweep entry Phase 3 left unresolved, call [eax+0x1c]): pe.json gives its byte-level target for every shape type - PLANE 0x00022dd0/phys_fn_001035(p3), SPHERE 0x00027c10/phys_fn_001373(p3), BOX 0x00020b20/phys_fn_000951(p5), CAPSULE 0x000225d0/phys_fn_001012(p3), MESH 0x00029610/phys_fn_001407(p3). Phase 3's 'never resolved' was behavioural, not byte absence; semantic identification still belongs to whichever phase picks the sweep up.",
  "Minor qualifying tables: phys_data_000976 @ 0x0010878c (8 slots, owner_phase 2) mixes four phase-5 targets with four filler slots; phys_data_000979 @ 0x00108818 (6 slots, owner_phase 2) mixes phases 6/7/5. No identity claimed.",
  "Files consulted: inventory.json; evidence/phase3-narrow-phase.md; gates/phase3.json; gates/phase3-closure.json; oracle/pe.json; oracle/data-coverage.json (pointer-table totals; its own 'vtables' and 'rtti' sections are EMPTY lists); oracle/ghidra/manifest.json + oracle/capstone/manifest.json (ctor vtable-store corroboration). Every required input existed EXCEPT the pinned oracle binary itself (pins.oracle.path), substituted by oracle/pe.json pointer records extracted from that same pinned image in Phase 1.",
  "Public headers under Physics/include were deliberately left unread: this census is structural and header declaration order was not needed to resolve RVAs. Header-order slot naming is the natural next step for whoever consumes this file."
